{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>עבר</b> — in the sense of pregnancy." "<b>יגעיל</b> — from the language of our Rabbis, of blessed memory: 'they scald it with boiling water.' The meaning is that the seed of the impurity will coagulate."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "He reads עבר as related to הריון (pregnancy), glossing the lemma as 'conceiving.'", 1 "The phrase מגעילן ברותחין is a talmudic expression; the final clause about זרע הקרי is textually difficult and rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:14.220527791Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}